				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "MwKSZKxxRb6TKIvnHHbDrg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Two languages, two debuggers! Both speak the Debug Adapter Protocol, which GT already speaks for Python, JavaScript, and gdb. That means we didn’t have to build a debugger UI at all, which is always nice."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "ps6trF8sTkWzj1K7OkRLsA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The first, {{gtClass:CarpDAPDebugger}}, debugs the language that runs while you compile. The Debug action on a snippet talks to the server in `--dap` mode, which records one expansion of the cell and lets us walk through it. Since we are walking a recording rather than a suspended interpreter, stepping backwards is just as cheap as stepping forwards. For now, it runs in a session of its own, so it can’t see macros defined elsewhere on the page yet."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "zgSLlaRXTu6DcW8sfhLmIw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The second, {{gtClass:CarpNativeDebugger}}, debugs the program a cell compiles to. Debug native builds the cell with debug information and starts `lldb-dap`, stopped where the cell’s own code begins. The compiler emits line directives that point back into the Carp source, and the debugger hides generated frames and variables and decodes mangled names. So when we step, we step through Carp, not through a pile of generated C."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "e2cwxjGvSoWRT0OZJ8LIIg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "This one rests on a whole tower of agreements between the compiler and GT: how names are mangled, what the line map looks like, how byte offsets become character positions. When one of them drifts, the debugger stops somewhere in C and stares at us blankly. `INVARIANTS.md` lists them all, and most of them don’t have an automated test yet. Native debugging is hard, y’all."
			}
		]
	},
